 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "A creature-only LOOK_AT_ENTITY step (a cod, a tropical fish) cannot be taught with 물고기: the concept has no `entity`, so the validator only accepts it when a condition mentions a biome tag (#minecraft:is_ocean). w4_01 had to watch a turtle, tactical_fishing watches the cod at sea (IN_BIOME ocean tag).",
  "HOLD_WHILE with an ACQUIRE_ITEM inner goal cannot be driven by PlaytestTest (the inner sub-tracker has no inventory baseline; status stays at 0/1), so meerestiefe s3 uses the HOLDING condition (same Korean, 낚싯대를 들고).",
  "A MOUNT step names its entity: only minecraft:oak_boat is known by the test fixtures (any other boat prints 동물), and (SIT, oak_boat) is the same (verb, object) pair for every MOUNT step, so the level-2 (verb, object) ratchet allows at most two more boat rides.",
  "(PLACE, lantern), (PLACE, torch), (KINDLE, campfire), (OBTAIN, water_bucket) and (GO, #minecraft:is_ocean) are saturated by earlier trails, so the harbour lights are copper lanterns and a jack-o'-lantern, and ocean trips name a special sea (따뜻한 바다, 깊은 바다, 미지근한 바다).",
  "The PLACE verb (놓다) is at the ratchet limit for level 2: placements were switched to 심다 (saplings, kelp, seagrass, cactus, sugar cane), 걸다 (banners), 깔다 (carpets) and 쌓다 where the object allows it.",
  "The ceremony generator prints seconds as digits (10초) while the authored clue says 십 초; w4_02 keeps an authored finale for that reason. Finale lines are authored only for tactical_fishing, axolotl, meerestiefe, ozeanfahrt and w4_02 so that the 70% generated-finale ratchet keeps slack (302 of 422 against 296).",
  "BETWEEN with a fluid as second anchor (모래와 물 사이에) is accepted by the validator but is not a placement a player can make for a plant that stands on the sand, so 사이에 is not practised in this batch.",
  "No concept names an island: 섬 was added as gen_island (descKo, tag by hand) and is spoken in one authored clue and in two finale lines; a REACH_BIOME step cannot ask for an island itself, only for its beach."
 ],
 "openIssues": [
  "formDependentShare.2 is 0.0938 -> 0.1464; this batch alone has 26 of 67 steps form-dependent (38.8%). HOLDING and 들고 are not form-dependent in the code, nor are PLAYER_REL conditions (판자 위에서 …).",
  "gen_island and gen_cod_bucket (and their two lexicon-tags.json entries) were written by hand because tools/curriculum/tag_lexicon.py needs the downloaded reference lists; a regeneration with the lists will rewrite them. 섬 is tagged without a curriculum band on purpose: as a core word it would add a never-met word to coverage.recycling.targetMetShare.",
  "The axolotl and the cod bucket are reachable in the first week only if a lush cave is found near the world spawn; the cave step is a real REACH_BIOME on minecraft:lush_caves.",
  "Reef (w4_01) uses seagrass, which needs shears; dolphins and the warm sea are found by boat (riffpfad)."
 ]
